<p>There’s an outer <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">TimelineView</code> that’s responsible for periodically triggering redraws of the inner view. The main content is the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Canvas</code> view.</p>

<p>For those with a UIKit background, the concept of a drawing context should be familiar: we get a canvas area with size information, then draw various elements on it — shapes, images, and more.</p>

<p>In our example, the particle to be drawn is represented by <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">SingleParticleView</code>. Note that it’s placed in the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">symbols</code> parameter — this means SwiftUI will <strong>pre-render</strong> it, making each subsequent draw call extremely efficient, which is great for large numbers of particles ;)</p>

